0..76 Comment "//! This fixture runs a migration model on two processes. Each process binds"
77..100 Comment "//! one declared world."
101..104 Comment "//!"
105..183 Comment "//! A world names a process only through the binding of its host, never in the"
184..261 Comment "//! source. Each migration to `far` runs in the process that binds `far`. The"
262..314 Comment "//! two migrations hold and read one value at `far`."
315..318 Comment "//!"
319..394 Comment "//! One process hosts `far` with `gandr host`, and another runs `main` with"
395..473 Comment "//! `gandr run`. Each process takes the binding `--world far=<key>@<ip:port>`,"
474..549 Comment "//! or the site and the manifold that the binding desugars from. The second"
550..625 Comment "//! migration reads a capture that the hosting process holds already. So no"
626..704 Comment "//! process fetches it. With no `--world` and no manifold, both migrations run"
705..745 Comment "//! in this process and answer the same."
746..749 Comment "//!"
750..797 Comment "//! - see: `crates/surface-driver/tests/net.rs`"
799..831 Comment "/// The world the entry runs at."
832..835 Keyword "pub"
836..841 Keyword "world"
842..846 Label "near"
846..847 Other ";"
849..919 Comment "/// The world the work runs at, in the process that its binding names."
920..923 Keyword "pub"
924..929 Keyword "world"
930..933 Label "far"
933..934 Other ";"
936..1012 Comment "/// `far` computes forty-two and holds it. A second migration reads it there"
1013..1023 Comment "/// again."
